<title>UK: Emotional depression carries high economic costs.</title>
<headline>Emotional depression carries high economic costs.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Emotional depression costs more than $43 billion a year in the U.S., but the cost could be cut dramatically by relatively inexpensive treatment, according to a report published on Tuesday.</p>
